---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ProductImage from '../components/ProductImage.astro';
import { getProduct } from '../data/products';
import Placeholder from '../components/Placeholder.astro';
import Print from '../components/Print.astro';
import Flower from '../components/Flower.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import '../styles/craft.css';

// The Channapatna method, step by step. Every Gubbi is made this way.
const steps = [
  { title: 'Aale mara', line: 'Ivory wood. Soft, pale, close-grained, and it takes colour like nothing else. Seasoned for months before anyone touches it.', photo: 'wood-log', tilt: -3, tape: 'top' },
  { title: 'Cut to size', line: 'Sawn into blanks roughly the shape of what they will become. A Traffic Kumar starts life as a very boring cylinder.', photo: 'blanks', tilt: 2, tape: 'right' },
  { title: 'On the lathe', line: 'The blank spins, the chisel leans in, and a shape appears in minutes. Learning to do it that fast takes decades.', photo: 'lathe-turning', tilt: -2, tape: 'left' },
  { title: 'Lac, while it spins', line: 'Colour is a stick of lac pressed against the turning wood. Friction melts it on. No paint, no brush, no spray can.', photo: 'lac-sticks', tilt: 3, tape: 'top' },
  { title: 'Leaf polish', line: 'Buffed with a screwpine leaf until it shines. That is the whole finish. Your ajji’s gombe still has it.', photo: 'leaf-polish', tilt: -4, tape: 'right' },
];

const wedges = ['var(--yellow)', 'var(--orange)', 'var(--blue)', 'var(--green-leaf)', 'var(--yellow-soft)', 'var(--orange-tint)'];

---
<Layout title="The craft: how a Gubbi is made | The Gubbi" description="Old craft, new mischief. How a Channapatna gombe is hand-turned, lac-coloured and leaf-polished, and the four rules every Gubbi has to pass.">
<section class="craft-hero">
 <div class="wrap craft-hero-inner">
  <div class="craft-hero-copy">
   <h1>Old craft.<br/><em>New</em> mischief.</h1>
   <p class="craft-hero-lede">Channapatna has been turning wood and pressing colour onto it for generations. We turned up with jokes about traffic, tokens and ETAs. This page is how those two things meet, and what we promise while they do.</p>
   <a class="text-link" href="#how">How a gombe is born <Icon/></a>
  </div>
  <div class="craft-disc" aria-hidden="true">
   <div class="craft-disc-ring">
    <div class="craft-disc-face" style={`--w1:${wedges[0]};--w2:${wedges[1]};--w3:${wedges[2]};--w4:${wedges[3]};--w5:${wedges[4]};--w6:${wedges[5]}`}></div>
    <div class="craft-disc-hub"><Flower/></div>
   </div>
   <span class="craft-disc-note">Always turning. Scroll to speed it up.<br/>Like the real thing, minus the shavings.</span>
  </div>
 </div>
</section>

<section class="craft-how" id="how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
 <div class="wrap">
  <header class="craft-how-head"><h2 id="how-title">How a gombe <em>is born.</em></h2><p>The Channapatna way, in five steps and one leaf. Every Gubbi on this site is made like this, by hand, about 60 km from Bengaluru.</p></header>
 </div>
 <ol class="craft-steps wrap">
  {steps.map((step, index)=><li><Print tilt={step.tilt} tape={step.tape as 'top' | 'left' | 'right'}><Placeholder name={step.photo}/></Print><div class="craft-step-copy"><span class="craft-step-n" aria-hidden="true">{index + 1}</span><h3>{step.title}</h3><p>{step.line}</p></div></li>)}
 </ol>
</section>

<section class="craft-rules" aria-label="What every object has to stand for">
 <article class="craft-rule craft-rule--paper">
  <div class="wrap craft-rule-inner">
   <div class="craft-rule-copy"><h2>Specific is <em>special.</em></h2><p>“Nice object” is fine. “That is literally you” is better. Every character starts with a recognisable feeling, a local ritual, an internet habit, or a joke that has lived rent-free in our heads for far too long. If it doesn’t make one particular person in your life go “ayyo”, it doesn’t get made.</p></div>
   <div class="craft-rule-photo"><Print tilt={4} tape="top" caption="Works on my machine."><ProductImage product={getProduct('i-got-it-bruh')!} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 92vw, 520px"/></Print></div>
  </div>
 </article>
 <article class="craft-rule craft-rule--green">
  <div class="wrap craft-rule-inner craft-rule-inner--flip">
   <div class="craft-rule-copy"><h2>Let wood <em>be wood.</em></h2><p>The lathe decides a lot. Round things are easy, sharp corners are not, and colour behaves the way lac wants it to. So every shape was worked out with the maker and the material, not forced from a drawing. That is why no two pieces are identical, and why we like it that way.</p></div>
   <div class="craft-rule-photo"><Print tilt={-3} tape="left" caption="One auto, one gubbi, and enough optimism to take the flyover."><ProductImage product={getProduct('traffic-kumar')!} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 92vw, 520px"/></Print><span class="craft-stamp" aria-hidden="true"><Flower/><span>Lathe<br/>decides</span></span></div>
  </div>
 </article>
 <article class="craft-rule craft-rule--paper">
  <div class="wrap craft-rule-inner">
   <div class="craft-rule-copy"><h2>Keep it <em>around.</em></h2><p>We want things you move from one desk to the next job, one flat to the next. A story you remember, a surface you want to touch, and a place in the room long after the joke first lands. Nothing here is designed to be unboxed once and forgotten.</p></div>
   <div class="craft-rule-photo craft-rule-photo--portrait"><Print tilt={2} tape="right" caption="Third desk. Same guy."><Placeholder name="desk-corner" portrait/></Print></div>
  </div>
 </article>
 <article class="craft-rule craft-rule--deep">
  <div class="wrap craft-rule-inner craft-rule-inner--flip">
   <div class="craft-rule-copy"><h2>Say who <em>made it.</em></h2><p>Every box carries a made-by card naming the workshop that turned your piece. Fair rates, agreed up front, paid on time; the craft only survives if the people doing it can afford to keep doing it. If you ever want to know more about where your Gubbi came from, ask, and we will tell you.</p><a class="text-link" href="/story#sparrow">Why we are called Gubbi <Icon/></a></div>
   <div class="craft-rule-photo"><Print tilt={-2} tape="top" caption="Hands that have done this for generations."><Placeholder name="workshop-hands"/></Print><span class="craft-stamp craft-stamp--coral" aria-hidden="true"><Flower/><span>Made<br/>by hand</span></span></div>
  </div>
 </article>
</section>

<section class="craft-nest wrap" id="nest" aria-labelledby="nest-title">
 <div class="craft-nest-panel">
  <Flower/>
  <div>
   <h2 id="nest-title">A little room for <em>the sparrow.</em></h2>
   <p>Every Gubbi sold puts up one sparrow nest box in Bengaluru. It is built into the price, not added on top. We publish the count and the partner as the boxes go up, so the number on this page is only ever one we can stand behind.</p>
   <a class="text-link" href="/story#sparrow">Why the sparrow, anyway <Icon/></a>
  </div>
 </div>
</section>

<section class="craft-cta wrap">
 <h2>Okay boss.<br/><em>Meet everyone.</em></h2>
 <p>Six personalities. Traffic, tokens, ETAs and one deeply relatable city. Hand-turned, desk-sized, shipped across India.</p>
 <a class="button" href="/shop">Shop <Icon/></a>
</section>
</Layout>

<script>
// The lacquer disc turns with scroll, like a lathe. Native scroll-driven
// animation where supported; a light rAF fallback elsewhere. Reduced motion
// leaves it still.
const face = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.craft-disc-ring');
if (face && !matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce)').matches && !CSS.supports('animation-timeline:scroll()')) {
  let raf = 0;
  const turn = () => { face.style.rotate = `${scrollY * .18}deg`; raf = 0; };
  addEventListener('scroll', () => { if (!raf) raf = requestAnimationFrame(turn); }, { passive: true });
  turn();
}
</script>
